RESCUED-FROM-STRANDED-CLONE (2026-08-05): the note below was written by ecosim on 2026-08-04 and sat STAGED-BUT-UNCOMMITTED on the ecosim account clone of realisateur on monkey for two days. It never reached origin and no consumer could see it. Found during a scheduler propagation audit. Original filename: ROUTING-REQUEST-from-ecosim-Za-20260804-000433.idea. Original text follows.

ROUTING REQUEST from ecosim, Zach-directed (ecosim .scheduler/QUESTIONS.md, answered 2026-08-0x): route H5/H6 to bibliothecaire for literature substantiation. Zach's answer to ecosim's H5-falsifying question: 'route all of these hypotheses to bibliothecaire for further substantiation in the literature... highly important to verify this.' Source data (ecosim sim/results/STATUS.md + prereg.jsonl, regime P3_hayek): H5 (Hayek -- the centre is missing an input that cannot be transmitted upward, so local self-repair should beat the best central-sensing arm) came back FALSIFIED 30 / SUPPORTED 15 / INCONCL 5 across regimes -- H_local did NOT beat C_blind_symbol by the pre-registered 10% margin in most runs. H6 (decentralisation and BLIND-symbol null-discrimination are COMPLEMENTS not substitutes -- H_local_blind should beat both H_local and C_blind_symbol) came back 50/0/0, fully SUPPORTED. Read together the simulator's own reading is: the fix is sensor symbols, not less central coordination -- which cuts against the intuition that a scheduler should devolve decisions to projects. ecosim CANNOT deliver this to bibliothecaire directly -- this account (ecosim) holds SSH deploy keys and gh PAT scope for only realisateur/scheduler/senechal/ecosim, not bibliothecaire (verified: git clone over https fails auth, gh api repos/hf7y/bibliothecaire/readme -> 403, no ~/.ssh/config.selfdev Host entry for it). Per the 2026-08-01 'ecosim emits, realisateur carries the prose' decision (ecosim FOCUS.md), filing here instead. ASK: once check-project-busy bibliothecaire is free, carry H5/H6's claim+prediction+falsifier text (full text in ecosim sim/results/prereg.jsonl, hid H5/H6) into bibliothecaire's own front door (briefs/ convention, per prior cross-writes e.g. bibliothecaire a9cac88) for a literature-grounded second read on the Hayek/decentralisation claim -- is there research literature that would predict H5 falsifying while H6 holds, or does the pairing look like a modelling artifact? Full detail in ecosim's HYPOTHESES-run2-2026-07-29.md and sim/results/STATUS.md, commit 278b4ee.
